message.content:
{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during your stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been having this sharp pain on my lower left side and back, and I keep needing to pee. It’s not like my usual stomach pain."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. Any fever, chills, or blood in the urine?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "No, no fever or blood. I did take some antibiotic a few days ago, but I don’t know what kind. It didn’t help much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. We’ll check your urine and run some blood tests. Your vital signs are stable, which is good."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve had these UTIs before. Could this be another one?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s possible. The pain being different from your usual abdominal pain makes us think it might be a complicated UTI."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Complicated? What does that mean?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It means the infection might involve the kidneys or there’s another factor, like your diabetes, that makes treatment harder."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, okay. I’m on insulin and have had trouble with infections before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we’ll keep a close eye on your blood sugar. We gave you some IV fluids, an anti-anxiety medicine, and pain relief in the ER."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I remember the lorazepam. It helped me relax. But the pain is still there."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll continue managing your pain. We also placed a temporary line in your groin because we couldn’t get a regular IV."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "The femoral line? I had one before. Is it safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2147-02-20 15:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s temporary. We’ll remove it once we get better access. We’re planning to place a PICC line tomorrow for longer treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2147-02-21 09:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. Your urine test showed a lot of white blood cells and bacteria. We sent a culture to see what kind."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2147-02-21 09:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will that tell you what antibiotic to use?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2147-02-21 09:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. We started you on Zosyn, which covers a broad range, but the culture will help us fine-tune it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2147-02-21 09:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been having some diarrhea too. Could that be from the antibiotic?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2147-02-21 09:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. We tested your stool for C. diff because of your history. The result came back negative."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2147-02-21 09:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So it’s not C. diff? I was worried about that."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2147-02-21 09:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "No, it’s not. The diarrhea is likely from the antibiotic. We’ll monitor it and keep you hydrated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2147-02-22 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re going to place the PICC line today. It’ll go into your arm and up to a large vein near your heart."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2147-02-22 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2147-02-22 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll get local numbing medicine. You might feel pressure, but it shouldn’t be painful."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2147-02-22 13:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The PICC line is in. A chest X-ray confirmed it’s in the right spot. We’ll use it to give your antibiotics."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2147-02-22 13:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. Does that mean I can go home soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2147-02-22 13:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not yet. You’ll need IV antibiotics for about 10 days. We’re arranging for you to go to a skilled nursing facility to finish the course."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2147-02-22 13:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, I see. I was hoping to go home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2147-02-22 13:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But with your diabetes and the severity of the infection, it’s safer to complete treatment with monitoring."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2147-02-23 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good news. Your urine culture grew Klebsiella pneumoniae, and it’s sensitive to the Zosyn we’re giving you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2147-02-23 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that a bad bug?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2147-02-23 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It can be, especially in people with diabetes. But since it’s responding to the antibiotic, we’re on the right track."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2147-02-23 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "My blood sugar has been high. Is that because of the infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2147-02-23 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, infections can raise blood sugar. We’re continuing your insulin and watching it closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2147-02-23 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been taking my Humalog with meals, but I haven’t eaten much."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2147-02-23 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good point. We’ll adjust your insulin if you’re not eating. We don’t want you going low."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2147-02-24 08:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white blood cell count is still high, but that’s expected with infection. It should come down with treatment."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2147-02-24 08:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my anemia? My hemoglobin is low again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2147-02-24 08:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s slightly low, but stable. We think it’s chronic, related to your other conditions. No need for transfusion."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2147-02-24 08:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been feeling tired. Is that from the anemia?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2147-02-24 08:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Partly. Infection and being in the hospital can also make you tired. You’re doing well overall."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2147-02-24 08:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I ate a big sandwich this morning. I thought my stomach couldn’t handle it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2147-02-24 08:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s a good sign! Your gastroparesis and GERD are still there, but you’re tolerating food better now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2147-02-24 08:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’m glad. I was worried I’d never eat normally again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Today’s the day. We’re discharging you to Vero Mattapan to finish your antibiotics through the PICC line."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. Will someone there take care of the line?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, the nurses will manage the IV and check your blood work every few days. Your PCP will follow up after."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my pain meds? I still have some discomfort."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You can continue tramadol, Lyrica, and the lidocaine patch. Keep using your omeprazole and sucralfate for your stomach."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the diarrhea?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It should improve once the antibiotics are done. Stay hydrated and let the facility know if it gets worse."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I feel better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve made good progress. Focus on finishing the antibiotics and taking care of your diabetes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I’ll see my doctor after this, right?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and we’ll send all your results to them. Call if you have fever, worsening pain, or line issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks for explaining everything."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. The nurse will go over your discharge papers and medications now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’m ready to get going."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2147-02-25 07:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Take care, and we’ll follow up with your PCP to make sure you’re healing well."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2147-02-20 14:42:00",
    "admission_end": "2147-02-25 11:12:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with a history of type 2 diabetes, chronic abdominal pain, gastroparesis, GERD, and recurrent UTIs was admitted with persistent urinary frequency and new-onset left lower quadrant and flank pain different from her usual symptoms. She had leukocytosis and a positive urine culture showing Klebsiella pneumoniae, confirming a complicated UTI. She received IV Zosyn and had a PICC line placed for outpatient antibiotic completion. Diarrhea developed during treatment but C. difficile testing was negative. Her pain was managed with tramadol, Lyrica, and other home medications. She tolerated oral intake well by discharge. Due to the need for extended IV antibiotics, she was discharged to a skilled nursing facility. Her diabetes, hypertension, depression, and anxiety were managed with home medications throughout the stay.",
    "problems": [
      "Urinary tract infection, site not specified",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Toxic gastroenteritis and colitis",
      "Type 2 diabetes mellitus with diabetic autonomic (poly)neuropathy",
      "Body mass index [BMI] 40.0-44.9, adult",
      "Long term (current) use of insulin",
      "Gastro-esophageal reflux disease without esophagitis",
      "Essential (primary) hypertension",
      "Major depressive disorder, single episode, unspecified",
      "Anxiety disorder, unspecified",
      "Other chronic pain",
      "Personal history of urinary (tract) infections",
      "Klebsiella pneumoniae [K. pneumoniae] as the cause of diseases classified elsewhere",
      "Adverse effect of unspecified systemic antibiotic, initial encounter",
      "Unspecified place in hospital as the place of occurrence of the external cause",
      "Obesity, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
